@talks pool
topic: home
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: shared pool, topic home. {home} is the roster's home ("Marra Station").

== smell
them: Something in the mess smelt like {home} today. Took me right back.
them: Funny what a smell can do. I had to sit down.
ask: Is there a smell that takes you home?
listen: What was it, the smell?
  them: Bread, I think. Or onions. Brennan wouldn't say which.   #funny
share: Rain on a warm street. Every time.
  them: You won't get that here. The garden's close, after watering.
cheer: Toast. Toast is always home.
  them: Then you're home three times a day. Lucky you.   #funny

== letter
them: Got a letter from {home}. Nothing much in it.
them: Read it three times anyway.   #warm
ask: Who writes to you from home?
listen: What was in it?
  them: The weather, a neighbour's new door, who's had a baby. Perfect.   #warm
share: My family. Not often enough.
  them: Write first. Short is fine. They'll write back faster.
cheer: Mostly people asking if I've eaten.
  them: Universal, that. Every home in the Concord asks it.   #funny

== first-night
them: My first night aboard, I lay awake listening to the ship.
them: Every hum sounded like something going wrong. None of it was.
ask: How did you sleep, your first night?
listen: When did it start feeling normal?
  them: About a week in. Then one night I just slept. Never looked back.
share: Badly. Lots of new noises.
  them: That's everyone. Give it a week. The hum turns into a lullaby.   #warm
cheer: Like a log. I was too tired to worry.
  them: The best way. Some people have all the luck.   #funny

== sky
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: Out here the sky's all stars. At {home} I mostly looked at the ground.   #funny
them: Puddles, mainly. Pavements. Now look at me.
ask: What was the sky like where you grew up?
listen: Do you miss looking down?
  them: A bit. You know where you are, looking down.
share: Big. You could see weather coming for miles.
  them: Weather. I'd forgotten weather. The ship has none.
cheer: Grey. Very grey. Excellent grey.
  them: Grey's underrated. It never shows off.   #funny

== cooking-home
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:brennan
them: There's a dish from {home} nobody aboard knows how to make.
them: I've described it to Brennan twice. She's thinking about it.
ask: What would you want from home, if Brennan could make anything?
listen: What's it like, this dish?
  them: Hot, cheap and better on a cold day. That's all a dish needs.
share: My family's one dish. Nobody else's.
  them: Tell Brennan. She keeps a book. She'll try, I promise.   #warm
cheer: All of it. One of everything.
  them: Brennan would take that as a challenge. Careful.   #funny

== street
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: You don't notice the little things till you're gone.
them: I could walk my old street with my eyes shut. Every crack.
ask: What do you remember best about where you grew up?
listen: What was on your street?
  them: A shop that sold everything badly. I loved it.   #funny
share: The people. Everyone knew everyone.
  them: Like the Wren, then. Seventy-odd people who know your business.   #funny
cheer: The shortcut to the bakery. Vital.
  them: Priorities. Good. Brennan does the bread here.   #funny

== both-homes
when: tier>=colleague rank:junior
them: Is it odd that the Wren feels like home now? Both at once?
them: I said "home" about my bunk the other day. Without thinking.
ask: Does the ship feel like home yet, for you?
listen: When did it change for you?
  them: I don't know. One day I was going "back to the ship". Then "home".
share: Getting there. Some days more than others.
  them: That's honest. It sneaks up on you. Then it's done.   #warm
cheer: It's got a canteen. That's most of home.
  them: Can't argue. A kitchen and people. That's it, really.   #funny

== leave-one-day
when: tier>=colleague
them: I'll go back to {home} on leave one day.
them: It'll all look smaller. People say it always does.
ask: What would you do first, back home?
listen: What would you do first?
  them: Walk. Just walk, somewhere without a corridor.   #warm
share: See my family. Sit at the kitchen table.
  them: Good answer. The kitchen table's where it all happens.   #warm
cheer: Sleep in a bed with no ladder.
  them: Ha! The upper bunk dream. Worth the trip alone.   #funny

== call-home
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: I called home last night. The line dropped twice.
them: We spent half the call saying "Can you hear me?"   #funny
ask: Have you called home yet, from the booths?
listen: Did you get to say what you wanted?
  them: Mostly. The important bit got through. That's the trick.
share: Yes. It helped more than I thought.
  them: It does. Even a short one. Go again this week.   #warm
cheer: I just shout louder. It's a method.
  them: Lag doesn't care how loud you are. Sadly.   #funny

== homesick
when: tier>=friend !newhere
them: Can I tell you something? I was very homesick my first month.
them: I hid it well. I think. I hope.   #serious
ask: Do you get homesick? You can say.
listen: What helped, in the end?
  them: Someone noticed and sat with me. Didn't fix it. Just sat.   #warm
share: Sometimes. In the evenings, mostly.
  them: Evenings are the worst. Find me, then. I'll sit with you.   #warm
cheer: Only when I see bread.
  them: Brennan has a lot to answer for.   #funny
